== Regional Transit-Pass Programmes

Several of the cities in which the firm maintains offices operate regional transit-pass programmes that reduce the administrative effort of repeated journeys. A pass removes the need to collect individual ticket receipts for every tram, metro, or regional train boarding, which in turn shortens the traveler's expense submission and Finance's review. Passes are approved when the intended pattern of travel makes them the sensible instrument, and the Travel Desk advises on the choice of zone and duration during trip planning. The approval decision is administrative, not discretionary: a pass covering the actual pattern of business travel will be endorsed, and a pass covering a wider area than the itinerary requires will be narrowed before booking.

